Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile a comprehensive report:

## Skill Section Analysis Report

Based on my exploration of the NINEONELABS renewal project, here's a complete technical breakdown of the homepage's skill/capability section (the "whyus" scene).

### 1. Full Skill Section HTML Markup

**Location:** `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/views/pages/index.php` (lines 260-300)

```html
<!--
SCENE: whyus
ARC: 전
PREVIOUS BEAT: who에서 우리의 역할과 파트너십의 방식이 분명해졌다.
CURRENT JOB: 그 역할을 실제로 수행할 수 있는 기술, 시스템, 역량을 증명한다.
VISUAL CONTEXT: 구조와 방향의 언어가 이제 도구와 실행력의 언어로 변환된다.
COPY RULE: 역량과 proof signal에 집중한다. 서비스 설명이나 브랜드 철학 반복으로 흐르지 않는다.
NEXT BEAT: services에서 실제로 무엇을 만들어내는지 구체적인 제공 항목을 보여준다.
-->
<section class="no-main-why" data-scene="whyus" aria-hidden="false">
    <div class="no-main-why__wrap">
        <div class="no-container">
            <div class="no-main-why__inner">
                <ul class="no-main-why__skill-list" data-why-skill-list>
                    <!-- Skill items generated via PHP loop -->
                </ul>
                <div class="no-main-why__preview" data-why-skill-preview aria-hidden="true">
                    <video class="no-main-why__preview-video" muted playsinline loop
                        data-why-skill-video></video>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
```

### 2. PHP Data Structure

**Location:** `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/views/pages/index.php` (lines 265-296)

**Skill Items Array:**
```php
$whySkills = [
    ['label' => 'THREE.JS',        'desc' => 'INTERACTIVE WEB'],
    ['label' => 'GSAP',            'desc' => 'MOTION & ANIMATION'],
    ['label' => 'WEBFLOW',         'desc' => 'NO-CODE BUILD'],
    ['label' => 'UI / UX DESIGN',  'desc' => 'USER EXPERIENCE'],
    ['label' => 'BRANDING SYSTEM', 'desc' => 'BRAND IDENTITY'],
    ['label' => '3D MODELING',     'desc' => 'SPATIAL DESIGN'],
    ['label' => 'SEO STRATEGY',    'desc' => 'SEARCH GROWTH'],
    ['label' => 'CMS SYSTEM',      'desc' => 'CONTENT CONTROL'],
];

$whyVideos = [
    '/resource/video/why_video_1.mp4',
    '/resource/video/why_video_2.mp4',
    '/resource/video/why_video_3.mp4',
    '/resource/video/why_video_4.mp4',
];
```

**Generated HTML for each skill item:**
```html
<li class="no-main-why__skill-item" data-why-skill-item
    data-skill-video="/resource/video/why_video_*.mp4">
    <span class="no-main-why__skill-label f-display-0 --semibold --fm-en-title">
        THREE.JS
    </span>
    <p class="no-main-why__skill-desc f-body-1 --regular" aria-hidden="true">
        INTERACTIVE WEB
    </p>
</li>
```

### 3. TypeScript Runtime Files

**Primary Component File:**
- **`/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/components/WhySkillPreview.ts`** (216 lines)
  - Exports `WhySkillPreview` class extending `Component`
  - Handles hover detection and video switching

**Key Files Referenced:**
- **`/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/config/component.config.ts`** (lines 104-117)
  - Configuration constants for WhySkillPreview
- **`/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/types/component.types.ts`** (lines 45-55)
  - Type definitions: `WhySkillPreviewOptions`, `WhySkillBinding`
- **`/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/runtime/PageRuntime.ts`** (lines 96-110)
  - Initialization hook that calls `WhySkillPreview.init()`
- **`/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/pages/main/scene/main.scene.ts`**
  - Main page Three.js scene setup with GSAP animations

### 4. SCSS Files

**Main Page Styles:**
- **`/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/scss/pages/_main.scss`** (lines 667-790)
  - Complete skill section styling

**Compiled Output:**
- **`/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/dist/css/`** (compiled CSS output)

### 5. Interaction Pattern: Hover Video Preview

The skill section implements a sophisticated **hover-based video preview system**:

#### **Trigger Points:**
1. **Hover Detection** (lines 98-104 in WhySkillPreview.ts):
   - `mouseenter` event on each skill item
   - `mouseleave` triggers delayed hide

2. **Video Switching Logic** (lines 107-168 in WhySkillPreview.ts):
   - When hovering skill item → loads video from `data-skill-video` attribute
   - **Cinematic video switch**: When switching between skills during active preview:
     - Sets `is-switching` class
     - Clips video with `clip-path: inset(50% 0 50% 0)` (vertical split effect)
     - 240ms transition to new video
     - Removes `is-switching` class to reveal new video
   - Queues pending video switches while animation is running (prevents jank)

3. **Position Tracking** (lines 136-140 in WhySkillPreview.ts):
   - Video preview positioned `fixed` at `top: 0`
   - `translateY(-50%)` centers vertically on the current skill item
   - Position updates via `getBoundingClientRect()` on enter

#### **Animation Timings (from component.config.ts):**
```typescript
WHY_SKILL_PREVIEW = {
  closeDelayMs: 120,        // Wait 120ms after mouseleave before hiding
  closeAnimationMs: 400,    // 400ms animation to hide video
  switchAnimMs: 240,        // 240ms to switch between videos
  visibleClass: 'is-visible',
  closingClass: 'is-closing',
  switchingClass: 'is-switching',
}
```

#### **Video States & CSS Classes:**
```html
<!-- Visible state -->
<div class="no-main-why__preview is-visible" data-why-skill-preview>
    <video ...></video>
</div>

<!-- Switching state (clips reveal during transition) -->
<div class="no-main-why__preview is-visible is-switching" ...>

<!-- Closing state (fades out) -->
<div class="no-main-why__preview is-closing" ...>
```

### 6. SCSS Styles Breakdown

**Location:** `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/scss/pages/_main.scss` (lines 667-790)

**Key CSS Classes & Transitions:**

```scss
// Skill list container
.no-main-why__skill-list {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 0;
  margin: 0;
  list-style: none;
  text-align: center;
}

// Individual skill item
.no-main-why__skill-item {
  position: relative;
  padding: fluid(10, 24) 0;
  cursor: default;
  transition: opacity var(--transition-base);
}

// Hover effect: dim other items
.no-main-why__skill-list:has(&__skill-item:hover) &__skill-item:not(:hover) {
  opacity: 0.2;
}

// Skill label (tech name)
.no-main-why__skill-label {
  display: block;
  line-height: 1;
}

// Skill description (hidden on desktop, shows on hover)
.no-main-why__skill-desc {
  position: absolute;
  right: 0;
  top: 50%;
  transform: translateY(-50%);
  margin: 0;
  opacity: 0;
  transition: opacity 0.24s ease;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.no-main-why__skill-item:hover &__skill-desc {
  opacity: 0.64;  // Reveal on hover
}

// Video preview container
.no-main-why__preview {
  position: fixed;
  top: 0;
  left: fluid(24, 56);
  transform: translateY(-50%);
  width: fluid(320, 560);
  aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
  overflow: hidden;
  opacity: 0;
  visibility: hidden;
  pointer-events: none;
  clip-path: inset(50% 0 50% 0);  // Initially hidden with clip
  transition:
    opacity 0.4s cubic-bezier(0.76, 0, 0.24, 1),
    visibility 0.4s cubic-bezier(0.76, 0, 0.24, 1),
    clip-path 0.48s cubic-bezier(0.76, 0, 0.24, 1),
    top 0.44s cubic-bezier(0.76, 0, 0.24, 1);
  z-index: 100;

  // Visible state
  &.is-visible {
    opacity: 1;
    visibility: visible;
    clip-path: inset(0% 0 0% 0);  // Fully reveal
  }

  // While switching videos (clip effect active)
  &.is-visible.is-switching {
    clip-path: inset(50% 0 50% 0);  // Re-clip during switch
  }

  // Closing animation
  &.is-closing {
    opacity: 0;
    clip-path: inset(50% 0 50% 0);
  }
}

// Video element
.no-main-why__preview-video {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  object-fit: cover;
  display: block;
}

// Mobile: hide video preview
@include mq(md) {
  .no-main-why__preview {
    display: none;
  }
}
```

### 7. Responsive Behavior

- **Desktop (lg breakpoint and above)**: 
  - Video preview visible on hover
  - Descriptions show with opacity: 0.64
  - Cinematic clip-path transitions active

- **Tablet/Mobile (md breakpoint and below)**:
  - Video preview hidden via `display: none`
  - Skill descriptions hidden entirely
  - Skill labels center-aligned

### 8. Technology Stack Summary

| Tech | Role | File |
|------|------|------|
| **Three.js** | Canvas background animation (separate from skill section) | `main.scene.ts` |
| **GSAP** | Timeline & animation orchestration for page scenes | `main.scene.ts` |
| **Webflow** | Referenced in skill list (no-code build capability) | index.php |
| **TypeScript** | Interactive skill preview component runtime | `WhySkillPreview.ts` |
| **SCSS** | Layout, transitions, clip-path animations | `_main.scss` |
| **Video** | 4 MP4 files (one per skill group) | `/resource/video/why_video_*.mp4` |

### Key Interaction Features

1. **Hover Detection**: Only fires on devices with hover capability (`ResponsiveRuntime.getDefault().getSnapshot().flags.hoverCapable`)
2. **Queue Management**: Prevents animation jank by queuing video switches during active animations
3. **Cinematic Transitions**: Uses CSS `clip-path` inset animation for smooth vertical reveal effect
4. **Auto Video Cycling**: Each skill item gets random video from pool of 4 videos
5. **Mobile Fallback**: Gracefully disables preview on touch devices
6. **Accessibility**: Video containers use `aria-hidden` attributes; descriptions have proper semantic markup

This implementation demonstrates advanced interactive patterns using vanilla TypeScript, CSS clip-path animations, and responsive detection—no jQuery or external animation libraries beyond GSAP for the broader page orchestration.

